# A battery, charger, backlight, LED, thermal zone or hwmon device that appears after boot (a
# late-probing driver, a hot-plugged charger) re-resolves /run/retroforge/hw. retroforge-hw.service is a
# plain oneshot, so systemd starts it again each time.
#
# Not for the coldplug replay (udevadm trigger marks its events with SYNTH_UUID; a kernel's own add
# has none): those devices are already in sysfs when the boot's own run of the service maps them,
# and tagging all of them made each one a pair of device units and an event PID1 had to process,
# 125 on the Air X (mostly LEDs), while the boot's first mounts and fsck waited behind them.
ENV{SYNTH_UUID}=="?*", GOTO="retroforge_hw_end"
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply|backlight|leds|thermal|hwmon", ACTION=="add", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="retroforge-hw.service"
LABEL="retroforge_hw_end"
